00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:21,000
Holiday Road is a tv movie, drama, romance film directed by Martin Wood.

2
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:36,000
A travel writer, a tech entrepreneur, a devoted mother and more strangers are stranded at
the airport for the holidays, they rent a van for an unexpected road trip.

3
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:51,000
Dana, played by Sara Canning.

4
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:06,000
Clay, played by Warren Christie.

5
00:26:15,000 --> 00:26:21,000
Tricia, played by Enid-Raye Adams.

6
00:31:30,000 --> 00:31:36,000
Ben, played by Kiefer O'Reilly.

7
00:36:45,000 --> 00:36:51,000
Ember Craig, played by Brittany-Ellen Willacy.

8
00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:06,000
Dusty Redford, played by Trevor Lerner.

9
00:47:15,000 --> 00:47:21,000
"Holiday Road" is a 1983 single composed and recorded by
American guitarist/singer Lindsey Buckingham.

10
00:52:30,000 --> 00:52:36,000
Written for the 1983 film National Lampoon's Vacation, it was also used in the film's sequels
National Lampoon's European Vacation (1985), Vegas Vacation (1997) and Vacation (2015).

11
00:57:45,000 --> 00:57:51,000
Despite only peaking at number 82 on the Billboard Hot 100 chart during its original
release, it has since become one of Buckingham's best known songs.

12
01:03:00,000 --> 01:03:06,000
Buckingham released a live version of the song on his 2008
album Live at the Bass Performance Hall.

13
01:08:15,000 --> 01:08:21,000
In July 2015, a remastered edition of "Holiday Road" was re-released, both on the Vacation soundtrack album and as a
digital download along with "Dancin' Across the USA" from the original National Lampoon's Vacation soundtrack.

14
01:13:30,000 --> 01:13:36,000
The film explores themes of holiday, based on true story, christmas.

15
01:18:45,000 --> 01:18:51,000
The tone is emotional.
